{
  "about": "The ink measurement's subject: two clusters of 21 record nodes, 178 relation edges, listed cluster A then cluster B. Every A node reaches four B nodes at fixed strides, so the cross edges run in four near-parallel families that a bundler has a reason to bundle; each cluster adds a path, a stride cycle and a fan from its first node, so there is long-span structure inside a cluster as well as across the gap. A graph, not a drawing: it carries no positions, and every layout is free to place it somewhere a bundler then has to cope with. Nothing here needs routing around anything: this is the bundling fixture, and the pairs that are meant to bundle are the ones a viewer would expect to see bundled.",
